  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale  \nThe strategy combines evolutionary search with constraint-handling techniques to explore the solution space beyond the symmetric construction of the provided `initial_h_values`. By iteratively improving candidate solutions through mutation, crossover, and selection, the method balances exploration and exploitation while respecting the problem's constraints.\n\n2. Mathematical specification  \n- Variables: h \u2208 [0, 1]^n, \u222bh dx = 1  \n- Objective: C\u2085 = max_k (h * (1 - h_k)) dx  \n- Constraints: h_i \u2208 [0, 1], \u2211h_i dx = 1  \n- Mutation: Add noise, clip, then scale to preserve sum  \n- Crossover: Weighted average with \u03b2 \u2208 [0, 1]  \n\n3. Implementation procedure  \na. Initialization:  \n- Read `initial_h_values` as starting point  \n- Generate population of 50 candidates by perturbing initial solution  \n\nb. Mutation:  \n- Add normal noise (\u03c3 = 0.1)  \n- Clip to [0,1]  \n- Scale to \u2211h = n/2, iterating until feasible  \n\nc. Crossover:  \n- Combine two parents with random weights  \n\nd. Selection:  \n- Binary tournament based on C\u2085 metric  \n\ne. Termination:  \n- Stop when time budget is exhausted or plateau detected  \n\n4. Search choices and useful variations  \n- Population size: 50  \n- Mutation noise: Normal distribution (\u03c3 adapts)  \n- Crossover rate: 0.5  \n\n5. Compute budget and robustness  \n- 50 evaluations per generation, 1100s allows ~1000 generations  \n- Feasibility maintained via iterative projection  \n\n6. Validation and return contract  \n- Ensure all h_i \u2208 [0,1] and \u2211h dx = 1  \n- Return best solution found",
